<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Storage problems anticipated.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Storage problems anticipated.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat basis bids were mostly steady on Friday with farmer selling light following recent price weakness.</p>
<p>Dealers noted growing concern about possible storage and transportation problems following a record Kansas wheat crop this year. Many farmers were seeking to clear out bins ahead of fall corn, sorghum and soybean harvests and move wheat to grain elevators.</p>
<p>There was talk that this year, some elevators were only taking wheat &quot;with no option for open storage&quot; with farmers having to commit to eventually selling them the wheat.  </p>
